// The text-change kind's steps (kinds/text-change.kind, N-865). coordd answers check_text, load_text and still_text
// itself, as the worker `coord`; read_text goes to whoever fills the role `text-reader` (by default the project's lead,
// policy/text-reader.eflint; others by the project's policy), the look's to the lead, and look_at to the agent that
// made the change.

// A file of the project's text as it is to be: PATH from the project's folder (`kinds/a.kind`, `calls/a.call`,
// `policy/a.eflint`, `renderings/a.tmpl`, `project.toml`, `standing.md`) or as the host has it, in the project's folder
// or its library; TEXT the whole of it, none to remove it. standing.md, the text every agent of the project starts
// with, is among the renderings, the project's prompt texts.
type TextFile {
  path: Text
  text: Text?
}

// The change applied to a copy of the project's text and read there as a reload reads it: refused with why and the
// places (file:line) when a file is not the project's text, a kind or call does not read, or an open ticket stands
// on what it changes; else the files (with BACK, the files as they were before that commit), who opened the change
// (BY: an agent's name, or `owner`, as the record has it), what each file touches, and READ, what the load holds them
// to: what they were when this check read them. Beside the folders' lists, what the check reads in the text: SHADOWS,
// the project's kinds named like one of agent-base's; BINDINGS, the bindings added, changed or gone (`on EVENT open`,
// `every`); HANDLERS, the kinds whose handlers of the owner's events (`when owner_...`) change. A change to the
// flavour's look alone is checked as the look and answered Look.
call check_text(files: [TextFile], back: Ref?) -> Checks(files: [TextFile], by: Text, kinds: [Text], calls: [Text], renderings: [Text], views: [Text], policy: [Text], library: [Text], shadows: [Text], bindings: [Text], handlers: [Text], read: Text) | Look(files: [TextFile], by: Text, read: Text) | Refused(why: Text, at: [Text])
  task check_text

// The checked files written, committed in the project's text repository and loaded, in one step: refused, with
// nothing written and no commit made, when a file is not what the check read or the load no longer passes.
call load_text(files: [TextFile], read: Text, why: Text) -> Live(commit: Ref) | Refused(why: Text, at: [Text])
  task load_text

// After the load, the picture the agent that made the change looks at (consult-lead, N-412 p1203): coordd starts a
// stand-in window, the window's own build (`window-stand-in` beside coordd), connected to this coordd as a watch as his
// window is, and it draws the page the change touches from what came on that link; for the look, once the look's
// event came on it. coordd chooses where the picture is written (the coord's `stills` folder, by ticket and step),
// never the request. STILL: its path, BY the agent that made the change, PAGE the page drawn. OWN: the owner made it,
// and his window draws it. UNSEEN: no window drew it, and why.
call still_text(files: [TextFile], commit: Ref) -> Still(path: Text, by: Agent, page: Text) | Own | Unseen(why: Text)
  task still_text

// The look at that picture by the agent that made the change: LooksRight, or Wrong with what is wrong, which takes
// the change back.
call look_at(why: Text, still: Text, page: Text) -> LooksRight | Wrong(what: Text)
  task look_at
  template
    Your change to this project's text is live: {{ why }}

    A window that took it as his window does drew {{ page }}: {{ still }}

    Open the picture and look at it as he would. Answer LooksRight when it shows what you meant, or Wrong with what is wrong: Wrong takes your change back, its files as they were before it.

// A change to the project's text, read before it goes live where the project's policy asks for it (`text-read`). BY
// made it; NAMES, what it touches as text-read's lists name them. Who reads it is whoever `fills` the step's role, and
// `fills` is given them: BY as `call.by`, each of NAMES as among(N, I) (paper-research N-1446 p2894).
call read_text(why: Text, by: Text, names: [Text], files: [TextFile]) -> Go | No(why: Text)
  task read_text
  template
    A change by {{ by }} to this project's own text asks for your read before it goes live: {{ why }}

    The files as they would be:
    {{ for f in files }}

    {{ f.path }}{{ if f.text }}:

    {{ f.text }}{{ end }}
    {{ end }}

    A file with no text is removed. Answer Go to make it live, or No with why to leave everything as it is.

// Whether a change to the project's text goes live at once (Go), is read first by the project's lead (Read),
// or is refused (No, why the rule's text). The policy sees who opened it (`call.by`) and each list's count
// (`call.X-count`), not its names.
decision text-read(by: Text, kinds: [Text], calls: [Text], renderings: [Text], views: [Text], policy: [Text], library: [Text], shadows: [Text], bindings: [Text], handlers: [Text]) -> Go | Read | No(why: Text)

// The same for a change to the flavour's look, the system's alone (policy/look.eflint).
decision look-read(by: Text) -> Go | Read | No(why: Text)
